.TH FULL 4 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
full \- always full device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/full
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B full
device behaves like
.B /dev/zero
when read, returning an endless supply of null bytes.
However, any attempt to write to
.B /dev/full
fails with the error
.B ENOSPC
(No space left on device).
.PP
This device is useful for testing how programs handle disk-full conditions.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOSPC
Returned for all write operations.
.SH EXAMPLE
Test error handling:
.PP
.nf
    echo "test" > /dev/full
    # Outputs: No space left on device
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dev/full
The full device special file (character device, major 1, minor 7).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR null (4),
.BR zero (4),
.BR intro (4)
